1
00:00:02,483 --> 00:00:06,072
Let me create an empty .dyno file.

2
00:00:06,072 --> 00:00:11,115
When I double click on it, it opens two views.

3
00:00:11,115 --> 00:00:13,621
On the left hand side, I can edit the model.

4
00:00:13,621 --> 00:00:15,658
Let's create a parameter beta.

5
00:00:15,658 --> 00:00:18,848
The arrow <- denotes an assignment.

6
00:00:18,848 --> 00:00:24,259
Let's define a second parameter r.

7
00:00:24,259 --> 00:00:27,261
Oops: definitions are evaluated in order!

8
00:00:27,261 --> 00:00:28,625
Let's move it to the second line.

9
00:00:28,625 --> 00:00:32,216
Now check out the preview panel.

10
00:00:32,216 --> 00:00:36,216
Both parameters are now defined.
